


# Code Coach commit message — write above these reminders.
#
# SUBJECT (first line, at most 50 characters)
# Summarize what changed. Start with a capitalized imperative verb:
# Add, Fix, Update, Remove, Refactor, Document, or Test.
# Do not end with a period. Leave one blank line before the body.
#
# BODY (required, wrap at 72 characters)
# Explain what changed and why it was needed, rather than how it works.
# Make the change type clear: feature, fix, refactor, docs, tests, etc.
# Cover the changes across all affected files without repeating the diff.
# Keep the explanation logical, complete, concise, and grammatical.
#
# Example only:
# Document contributor message conventions
#
# Add commit and PR templates to remind contributors to explain each
# change and its motivation, making the work easier for teammates to review.
#
# CI checks message formatting. Git's default cleanup removes these
# reminders from editor-based commit messages.
